  "stationary_reference": {
    "law": "x[t] = a*x[t-1] + b*u[t] + eta[t], |a|<1",
    "assumptions": "Independent zero-mean input u and other drive eta, both temporally iid with finite variances, fixed coefficients, stationary state; no saturation, cancellation, learned graph or activity-dependent controller.",
    "derivation": [
      "Var(x)=(b^2*Var(u)+Var(eta))/(1-a^2)",
      "Cov(x[t],u[t-k])=b*a^k*Var(u)",
      "Squared correlation R_k^2 = b^2*Var(u)*(1-a^2)*a^(2k)/(b^2*Var(u)+Var(eta))",
      "The optimum scalar linear reconstruction has explained-variance fraction R_k^2. Summing k>=0 gives b^2*Var(u)/(b^2*Var(u)+Var(eta)), independent of a.",
      "For fixed k>0, maximizing (1-a^2)*a^(2k) over 0<=a<1 gives a^2=k/(k+1). This is lag-specific, not a universal optimal gain."
    ],
